                    <rect x="65" y="115" width="40" height="20" rx="10" fill="#FFE0B2" stroke="#2d2d44" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <rect x="195" y="115" width="40" height="20" rx="10" fill="#FFE0B2" stroke="#2d2d44" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <rect x="120" y="225" width="20" height="80" rx="10" fill="#FFE0B2" stroke="#2d2d44" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <rect x="160" y="225" width="20" height="80" rx="10" fill="#FFE0B2" stroke="#2d2d44" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <rect x="115" y="155" width="70" height="50" rx="10" fill="#ff6b6b" stroke="#2d2d44" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <text x="150" y="185" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="white">PRIVATE</text>
                    <text x="150" y="350" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#ff6b6b">🚫 NO ONE SHOULD TOUCH THE RED AREA</text>
                    <text x="150" y="370" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#6b6b80">Your body belongs to YOU</text>
                </svg>
                <p class="diagram-caption">The "Swimsuit Rule": The parts covered by a swimsuit are private.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="highlight-box"><strong>Remember:</strong> Bad touch is <em>never</em> your fault. Even if the person is a relative, a teacher, or someone you know. It is always the adult's fault, not yours.</div>
            <p>If someone gives you a bad touch, <strong>say NO loudly, run away, and tell a trusted adult immediately</strong>.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- PANTS -->
        <div id="pants" class="story-panel hidden">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-shield-alt" style="color:var(--primary);"></i> The PANTS Rule</h3>
            <p>The PANTS rule is a simple way to remember how to keep your body safe. It works for every child.</p>
            <div class="pants-diagram">
                <div class="pants-item"><div class="letter">P</div><h4>Privates are private</h4><p>The parts of your body covered by underwear are private. No one should ask to see or touch them.</p></div>
                <div class="pants-item"><div class="letter">A</div><h4>Always remember your body belongs to you</h4><p>You are the boss of your body.</p></div>
                <div class="pants-item"><div class="letter">N</div><h4>No means no</h4><p>If someone asks you to do something you don't like, you can say NO.</p></div>
                <div class="pants-item"><div class="letter">T</div><h4>Talk about secrets that upset you</h4><p>If a secret makes you feel scared or sad, you <em>must</em> tell a trusted adult.</p></div>
                <div class="pants-item"><div class="letter">S</div><h4>Speak up — someone can help</h4><p>If you are worried or scared, tell a parent, teacher, or another adult you trust.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="warning-box"><strong>Exception:</strong> Sometimes a doctor or nurse may need to check your private parts, but only with your parents with you, and they should explain why.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Cyber -->
        <div id="cybersafety" class="story-panel hidden">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-mobile-alt" style="color:var(--primary);"></i> Cyber Safety</h3>
            <div class="diagram-container">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 400 300" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Cyber safety phone diagram">
                    <rect x="120" y="20" width="160" height="260" rx="20" fill="#2d2d44" stroke="#2d2d44" stroke-width="3"/>
                    <rect x="130" y="35" width="140" height="220" rx="8" fill="#e8faf8"/>
                    <text x="200" y="70" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#2d2d44">🛡️ Stay Safe!</text>
                    <text x="160" y="110" font-size="20">🚫</text><text x="190" y="110" font-size="11" fill="#2d2d44">Don't share info</text>
                    <text x="160" y="140" font-size="20">🔒</text><text x="190" y="140" font-size="11" fill="#2d2d44">Keep passwords secret</text>
                    <text x="160" y="170" font-size="20">👤</text><text x="190" y="170" font-size="11" fill="#2d2d44">Tell a trusted adult</text>
                    <text x="160" y="200" font-size="20">📞</text><text x="190" y="200" font-size="11" fill="#2d2d44">Call 1930 if scared</text>
                    <text x="200" y="250" text-anchor="middle" font-size="30">🛡️</text>
                </svg>
                <p class="diagram-caption">Remember: The internet is like a big city. Stay with people you trust.</p>
            </div>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Never share your full name, address, school, or phone number</strong> with strangers online.</li>
                <li><strong>Do not share your passwords</strong> with anyone except your parents.</li>
                <li><strong>If someone sends you a message that makes you feel uncomfortable</strong>, do not reply. Show it to a parent or teacher immediately.</li>
                <li><strong>Never meet an online friend alone.</strong> Always tell your parents if someone asks to meet you.</li>
                <li><strong>Report cyberbullying or bad messages</strong> to the Cyber Crime helpline <strong>1930</strong> or visit <strong>cybercrime.gov.in</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="highlight-box">The National Cyber Crime Helpline (<strong>1930</strong>) is free and available 24/7. You can also file a complaint online at <strong>cybercrime.gov.in</strong>.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Trusted Adults -->
        <div id="trustedadults" class="story-panel hidden">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-user-friends" style="color:var(--primary);"></i> Trusted Adults & Safety Circle</h3>
            <div class="diagram-container">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Safety circle diagram">
