                    <text x="320" y="150" text-anchor="middle" font-size="30">👨</text><text x="320" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#2d2d44">Father</text>
                    <text x="80" y="150" text-anchor="middle" font-size="30">👵</text><text x="80" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#2d2d44">Grandma</text>
                    <text x="320" y="270" text-anchor="middle" font-size="30">👮‍♀️</text><text x="320" y="290" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#2d2d44">Police</text>
                    <text x="80" y="270" text-anchor="middle" font-size="30">👩‍🏫</text><text x="80" y="290" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#2d2d44">Teacher</text>
                    <text x="200" y="380" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#6b6b80">These are your safety circle helpers</text>
                </svg>
                <p class="diagram-caption">Your Safety Circle: people you can trust and talk to.</p>
            </div>
            <p>A <strong>trusted adult</strong> is someone you feel safe with. They listen to you and believe you. Examples: your mother, father, grandmother, teacher, school counsellor, or a police officer.</p>
            <div class="highlight-box"><strong>Important:</strong> If the first adult you tell does not believe you, <em>tell another trusted adult</em>. Keep telling until someone helps you. You deserve to be heard.</div>
            <p><strong>Childline (1098)</strong> is a free, 24/7 helpline for children. You can call them if you are scared, hurt, or need help.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Consent -->
        <div id="consent" class="story-panel hidden">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-hand-paper" style="color:var(--primary);"></i> My Body, My Rules</h3>
            <p><strong>Consent</strong> means asking before you do something that involves another person's body. It means respecting when someone says "no."</p>
            <ul>
                <li>You have the right to say <strong>NO</strong> to any touch that makes you uncomfortable — even to a family member.</li>
                <li>You do not have to hug or kiss anyone if you don't want to.</li>
                <li>Your body is yours. No one has the right to touch you in a way that makes you feel bad.</li>
                <li>If someone touches you without your permission, <strong>it is not your fault</strong>. Tell a trusted adult immediately.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="warning-box"><strong>Real example:</strong> If someone asks you to sit on their lap and you don't want to, you can say "No, thank you." You are allowed to say no.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Secrets -->
        <div id="secrets" class="story-panel hidden">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-user-secret" style="color:var(--primary);"></i> Safe vs. Unsafe Secrets</h3>
            <p><strong>Safe secrets</strong> are fun — like a surprise birthday party or a gift. They make you feel happy.</p>
            <p><strong>Unsafe secrets</strong> make you feel scared, worried, or sick to your stomach. If an adult tells you to keep a secret about touching or something that feels wrong, <strong>that is an unsafe secret</strong>.</p>
            <div class="highlight-box"><strong>Rule:</strong> You should <em>never</em> keep a secret that makes you feel uncomfortable. Tell a trusted adult right away, even if the person said you would get in trouble. You will <em>not</em> get in trouble.</div>
        </div>

