    <!-- ================= CASE STUDIES ================= -->
    <div id="casestudies" class="section">
        <div class="section-title"><i class="fas fa-gavel"></i> Real Stories & Case Studies</div>
        <p class="section-sub">These are real cases from Tamil Nadu and around the world. They show why speaking up and knowing the law matters.</p>

        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">Tamil Nadu · 2025</span><h4>⚖️ Tirunelveli POCSO Case — Death Penalty for Father</h4><p>A POCSO court in Tirunelveli sentenced a 47-year-old man to death for sexually assaulting and impregnating his 14-year-old daughter. The court called it a "heinous and unforgivable crime" and ordered the state to pay ₹10 lakh compensation to the survivor.</p></div>
        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">Tamil Nadu · 2025</span><h4>⚖️ Tiruvarur POCSO Case — 54 Years for Woman Offender</h4><p>A 38-year-old anganwadi worker was sentenced to 54 years of rigorous imprisonment for abducting and sexually assaulting a Class X student in Tiruvarur. This shows the POCSO Act is <strong>gender-neutral</strong>.</p></div>
        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">Tamil Nadu · 2025</span><h4>⚠️ Nilgiris School Case — 21 Girls Harassed</h4><p>A science teacher at a government school in the Nilgiris was arrested for sexually harassing 21 girl students. The abuse came to light after police conducted an awareness session on "good touch and bad touch" at the school.</p></div>
        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">India · 2012</span><h4>⚖️ The Nirbhaya Case — A Turning Point for India</h4><p>In December 2012, a 23-year-old physiotherapy student was gang-raped on a moving bus in New Delhi. The case sparked nationwide protests and led to major legal reforms, including the Criminal Law (Amendment) Act, 2013.</p></div>
        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">Panchkula · 2025</span><h4>🏫 School Workshop Empowers Teen to Report Abuse</h4><p>A 14-year-old girl in Panchkula found the courage to report an auto driver who had been molesting her — <strong>because she attended a school workshop on "good touch and bad touch"</strong>.</p></div>
        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">Bangladesh · BRAC Schools</span><h4>🌍 "Shapla's Story" — 20 Minutes That Saved a Child</h4><p>Eight-year-old Shapla escaped an assault because she remembered her teacher's 20-minute lesson on bad touch. BRAC's programme teaches the "Bathing Suit Rule" and the "No, Go, Tell" action plan.</p></div>
        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">Tamil Nadu · 2025</span><h4>🛡️ NIMIR Police Team — Child-Friendly Policing</h4><p>A special police team in Tamil Nadu called <strong>NIMIR</strong> travels across the district to educate children about sexual offences and good/bad touch.</p></div>
        <div class="case-card"><span class="case-tag">Chennai · 2025</span><h4>📚 Private School POCSO Guidelines</h4><p>The Directorate of Private Schools in Chennai issued guidelines requiring POCSO training for all staff, parent awareness sessions on good touch and bad touch, and the formation of a safeguarding committee in every school.</p></div>
    </div>

    <!-- ================= LEGAL ================= -->
    <div id="legal" class="section">
        <div class="section-title"><i class="fas fa-balance-scale"></i> Your Legal Rights (Simple Words)</div>

        <div class="legal-card"><h4>POCSO Act, 2012 — Protection of Children from Sexual Offences</h4><p>This law protects all children under 18 from sexual abuse. It is <strong>gender-neutral</strong>. The Act includes child-friendly procedures like in-camera trials and no aggressive questioning. Convictions have included the death penalty and consecutive life sentences.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-card"><h4>Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act, 2005</h4><p>This law protects women from physical, emotional, verbal, sexual, and economic abuse at home. Women can get protection orders, residence orders, and monetary relief. Tamil Nadu has Protection Officers in every district — Chennai: 9786527453; Coimbatore: 9865432109.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-card"><h4>Sexual Harassment at Workplace (PoSH) Act, 2013</h4><p>Every workplace with 10 or more employees must have an Internal Complaints Committee (ICC). If you face harassment at work, you can complain to the ICC.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-card"><h4>Free Legal Aid — You Don't Need Money</h4><p>Women and children are automatically eligible for free legal services. Call the National Legal Aid Helpline <strong>15100</strong> or the Tamil Nadu State Legal Services Authority at <strong>1800 4252 441</strong> or <strong>044-25342441</strong>. Email: <strong>tnslsa@gmail.com</strong>.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-card"><h4>Child Marriage is Illegal</h4><p>Under the Prohibition of Child Marriage Act, 2006, marrying a girl below 18 or a boy below 21 is a crime. You can report it to <strong>1098</strong> (Childline) or <strong>112</strong>.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-card"><h4>Missing Women & Children — Helpline 1094</h4><p>If a woman or child goes missing, call <strong>1094</strong> immediately. This is a dedicated Tamil Nadu helpline for missing persons.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-card"><h4>Transgender Rights — TN Policy 2025</h4><p>Tamil Nadu's 2025 Transgender Policy affirms the right to self-identify gender without medical certification, establishes a 24/7 helpline, provides free legal aid, and offers counselling for parents.</p></div>
        <div class="legal-card"><h4>Cybercrime Reporting — Your Right</h4><p>You can file a cybercrime complaint anytime at <strong>www.cybercrime.gov.in</strong> or by calling <strong>1930</strong>. The Tamil Nadu government has issued a digital safety rulebook, "Guiding Light," for girl students.</p></div>
    </div>

